                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm not sure what to say. It's a fascinating idea - a virtual gallery for virtual artworks that predated the current wave of VR. \n\nBut some of the art on display is truly awful. It's like the throwaway experiments you produce when you're running through a tutorial for a 3D modelling app - but given a portentious name and some verbose waffle about it's meaning. I'm not going to name names - not all the work on display is terrible - but the terrible stuff is so bad it's hard to take the whole thing seriously afterwards.\n\nI like the idea of displaying digital art in VR - but someone needs to do some quality control. And lose the vacuous verbiage that accompanies it.",
